 "issue": 1306,
 "issue_title": "Bug: auto_clean() returns undocumented tuple when dry_run=True and return_report=True are combined \u2014 violates type annotation and docstring contract",
 "issue_body": "### What happened?\n\n`auto_clean()` silently returns a `tuple` instead of `DataQualityReport` when \n`dry_run=True` and `return_report=True` are passed together.\n\nNo error is raised. The caller receives a tuple and any attempt to use it as a \nDataQualityReport crashes with:\n\nAttributeError: 'tuple' object has no attribute 'quality_score'\n\nThe docstring documents no return value for this combination. The very similar \n`explain=True + dry_run=True` combination correctly raises a ValueError \u2014 but \n`return_report=True + dry_run=True` silently returns garbage instead.\n\n### Area\n\nData profiling / quality reports\n\n### Minimal reproduction\n\nimport arnio as ar\nimport pandas as pd\n\nframe = ar.from_pandas(pd.DataFrame({\"name\": [\" Alice \", \" Bob \"]}))\nresult = ar.auto_clean(frame, dry_run=True, return_report=True)\n\nprint(type(result))\n# \u274c <class 'tuple'>  \u2014 Expected: DataQualityReport\n\nresult.quality_score\n# \u274c AttributeError: 'tuple' object has no attribute 'quality_score'\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n<html>\n<body>\n<!--StartFragment--><html><head></head><body><h1>\ud83d\udc1b <code>auto_clean()</code> Silently Returns Wrong Type \u2014 <code>dry_run=True</code> + <code>return_report=True</code></h1>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>File:</strong> <code>arnio/quality.py</code> \u00b7 <strong>Function:</strong> <code>auto_clean()</code> \u00b7 <strong>Severity:</strong> \ud83d\udd34 Medium-High \u00b7 <strong>Labels:</strong> <code>bug</code> <code>api</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>What's Wrong</h2>\n<p>Calling <code>auto_clean()</code> with <strong>both</strong> <code>dry_run=True</code> and <code>return_report=True</code> silently returns a <code>tuple</code> instead of the documented <code>DataQualityReport</code> \u2014 <strong>no error raised, no warning given.</strong></p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Reproduce in 10 seconds</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">import arnio as ar\nimport pandas as pd\n\nframe = ar.from_pandas(pd.DataFrame({\"name\": [\" Alice \", \" Bob \"]}))\n\nresult = ar.auto_clean(frame, dry_run=True, return_report=True)\n\nprint(type(result))\n# \u274c &lt;class 'tuple'&gt;\n# \u2705 Expected: &lt;class 'arnio.quality.DataQualityReport'&gt;\n\nresult.quality_score\n# \u274c AttributeError: 'tuple' object has no attribute 'quality_score'\n</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h2>Root Cause</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\"># arnio/quality.py \u2014 inside auto_clean()\n\nif dry_run:\n    if return_report:\n        return frame, report   # \ud83d\udc1b returns tuple \u2014 undocumented, wrong, untested\n    return report              # \u2705 correct path\n</code></pre>\n<p>The <code>return_report</code> flag makes no sense in a <code>dry_run</code> \u2014 no cleaning happens, so returning the original frame alongside the report is meaningless. Meanwhile, the <strong>very similar</strong> <code>explain + dry_run</code> combination was correctly guarded:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">if dry_run and explain:\n    raise ValueError(\"explain=True cannot be used with dry_run=True\")  # \u2705 guarded\n\nif dry_run and return_report:\n    # \u274c NOT guarded \u2014 silently misbehaves\n</code></pre>\n<p><strong>Inconsistent. One raises. The other returns garbage silently.</strong></p>\n<hr>\n<h2>What the Docs Promise vs Reality</h2>\n\nCall | Documented Return | Actual Return\n-- | -- | --\nauto_clean(frame, dry_run=True) | DataQualityReport | DataQualityReport \u2705\nauto_clean(frame, dry_run=True, return_report=True) | (not documented) | tuple \u274c\n\n\n<hr>\n<h2>Fix (3 lines)</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\"># Add alongside the existing explain guard:\nif dry_run and return_report:\n    raise ValueError(\n        \"return_report=True cannot be used with dry_run=True. \"\n        \"dry_run already returns the DataQualityReport directly.\"\n    )\n</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h2>Missing Tests</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">def test_auto_clean_dry_run_with_return_report_raises():\n    frame = ar.from_pandas(pd.DataFrame({\"name\": [\" Alice \"]}))\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"return_report=True cannot be used with dry_run=True\"):\n        ar.auto_clean(frame, dry_run=True, return_report=True)\n\ndef test_auto_clean_dry_run_never_returns_tuple():\n    frame = ar.from_pandas(pd.DataFrame({\"name\": [\" Alice \"]}))\n    result = ar.auto_clean(frame, dry_run=True)\n    assert isinstance(result, ar.DataQualityReport)\n    assert not isinstance(result, tuple)\n</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Fix complexity:</strong> \u2b50 Easy \u2014 3 lines + 2 tests\n<strong>Found during:</strong> GirlScript Summer of Code \u2014 <code>arnio/quality.py</code> code review</p>\n</blockquote></body></html><!--EndFragment-->\n</body>\n</html>\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n>>> result = ar.auto_clean(frame, dry_run=True, return_report=True)\n\n>>> print(type(result))\n<class 'tuple'>        # \u274c should be DataQualityReport\n\n>>> result.quality_score\nAttributeError: 'tuple' object has no attribute 'quality_score'\n\n>>> print(result)\n(<ArFrame ...>, DataQualityReport(row_count=2, ...))\n# Returns (ArFrame, DataQualityReport) tuple \u2014 undocumented, unexpected\n\n### Impact\n\nBlocks installation or import\n\n### Arnio version\n\nRun this in your terminal and paste the output: python -c \"import arnio; print(arnio.__version__)\"\n\n### Install method\n\npip install -e .\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux\n\n### Python version\n\nRun this and paste the output: python --version\n\n### Environment details\n\n```shell\n\n```\n\n### Pre-flight checks\n\n- [x] I searched existing issues and did not find a duplicate.\n- [x] I included a minimal reproduction or explained why one is not possible.\n\n### Additional context\n\nRoot cause is in arnio/quality.py inside auto_clean():\n\n    if dry_run:\n        if return_report:\n            return frame, report   # \u2190 BUG: returns tuple silently\n        return report              # \u2190 correct path\n\nThe explain + dry_run combination was correctly guarded:\n\n    if dry_run and explain:\n        raise ValueError(\"explain=True cannot be used with dry_run=True\")\n\nBut return_report + dry_run was never guarded \u2014 same pattern, inconsistent behavior.\n\nProposed fix (3 lines):\n\n    if dry_run and return_report:\n        raise ValueError(\n            \"return_report=True cannot be used with dry_run=True. \"\n            \"dry_run already returns the DataQualityReport directly.\"\n        )\n\nMissing tests:\n- auto_clean(frame, dry_run=True, return_report=True) is never tested in test_quality.py\n- No test asserts that dry_run result is never a tuple",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1306",
